{"availability":"available","full":"tgmaurer/dotdown","name":"dotdown","description":"A countdown to one date, shown as a grid of dots. No account, no tracking: the whole countdown lives in the link.","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-02T14:08:12Z","updated":"2026-10-13T19:17:10Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://tgmaurer.github.io/dotdown/","topics":["countdown","github-pages","javascript","privacy","vanilla-js"],"demo":"https://tgmaurer.github.io/dotdown/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T22:40:26.872Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T22:40:26.872Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T22:40:26.872Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T07:03:55.835Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-15T23:46:30.440Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-17T22:40:26.872Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A tiny countdown to one date. Give it a name and a target date and it shows the days, hours, minutes and seconds that are left, plus one small square for every day of the span, so you can watch the deadline shrink. You can attach a short list of goals. It is not a task tracker.","There is no backend, no account, no build step and no dependency. It is three plain files (index.html, style.css, app.js), a service worker (sw.js) that keeps an offline copy for fast launches, a privacy page (privacy.html), two icons and one font file (Commit Mono, served from fonts/), and it makes no third-party requests."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tgmaurer/dotdown/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"30fb266b420551d6596fa67bc25121a532e2dfc03b9e5ce69e27dd417ecbf801","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T07:03:55.941Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T22:40:26.964Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A tiny countdown to one date. Give it a name and a target date and it shows the days, hours, minutes and seconds that are left, plus one small